_model: proposition
---
title: Proposition 13
---
order: 13
---
short_label: III.13
---
statement: A circle does not touch another circle at more than one point whether it touches it internally or externally.
---
proof:

For, if possible, let the circle *ABDC* touch the circle *EBFD,* first internally, at more points than one, namely *D* and *B.*

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="260" height="250" tabindex="0"></canvas>
